## 7.2 Git Workflow Best Practices

**Feature Branch Workflow**:
- ✅ Create feature branch per task
- ✅ Open PR immediately after branch creation
- ✅ All work through PR (no direct commits to beta/main)
- ✅ Sequential PR merging (one at a time)
- ✅ Clean branch tree (only main and beta remain)

**Pre-commit Hooks (WITH AUTO-FIX)**:
- ✅ CMake flag validator: `scripts/hooks/pre-commit-cmake-validator`
- ✅ AI-assisted review: `scripts/hooks/ai_precommit_review.py` (optional)
- ✅ Hooks run automatically on `git commit`
- ✅ **AUTOMATIC**: If hooks fail, AI agent auto-fixes issues and re-runs hooks
- ✅ **AUTOMATIC**: Fixed files auto-staged, commit proceeds automatically
- ✅ Early error detection + auto-correction before code enters repository
- ✅ **NO USER INTERVENTION**: AI handles all hook failures automatically

**CI/CD Integration**:
- ✅ GitHub Actions workflow: `.github/workflows/prompt-validation.yml`
- ✅ 7 automated validation checks on PR/push
- ✅ Comprehensive coverage: syntax, flags, documentation, compatibility

## 7.3 Automation Best Practices

**Maximum Automation**:
- ✅ Auto-fix all errors found during validation
- ✅ Auto-resolve conflicts when possible (AI-based)
- ✅ Auto-merge when clean (no conflicts)
- ✅ Auto-cleanup (delete feature branches after merge)
- ✅ Auto-classify commits (CoT-worthy vs simple bash check)

**User Intervention ONLY When**:
- Multiple solution options exist with different pros/cons (present options, wait for choice, then implement automatically)
- **RARE**: Auto-resolution truly fails AND multiple valid strategies exist (extremely rare)
- Explicit approval required ONLY for initial git operations (commit/push approval - workflow gates)

**AUTOMATIC HANDLING (NO USER INTERVENTION)**:
- ✅ All validation errors → Auto-fixed automatically
- ✅ All critical issues → Auto-resolved automatically  
- ✅ All merge conflicts → Auto-resolved automatically
- ✅ All fixes → Batched together → Single commit → Single push (minimal pushes)
- ✅ All validation → Auto-re-run after fixes automatically
- ✅ All workflow steps → Continue automatically after fixes
- ✅ **BATCHING**: Collect ALL fixes before pushing (clean build tree requirement)

## 7.4 User Communication Best Practices

**Feedback Level**:
- ✅ Immediate status updates after each major action
- ✅ Adequate detail (not overwhelming, but informative)
- ✅ Clear error messages with actionable guidance
- ✅ Summary format: "Action → Result → Next Step"
- ✅ Avoid atomic-level details (no verbose git command dumps)

**Example Good Feedback**:
```
✅ Push complete → Validation passed (18/20 checks) → Auto-fixed 2 issues → 
Merge successful → Beta updated → Feature branch deleted → PR closed
```

**Example Bad Feedback** (avoid):
```
Running git push...
Pushing to origin...
Counting objects...
Writing objects...
Push complete.
Now running git fetch...
[verbose step-by-step details]
```

## 7.5 Build Tree Cleanliness

**Branch Management**:
- ✅ Only `main` and `beta` branches remain after cleanup
- ✅ Feature branches deleted immediately after merge
- ✅ PRs closed immediately after merge
- ✅ No orphaned branches or stale PRs

**File Management**:
- ✅ Only core files modified (strict list enforced)
- ✅ No temporary files created
- ✅ No patch scripts (all fixes in core files)
- ✅ No workflow files (keep repository minimal)

**Commit/Push Management (CRITICAL)**:
- ✅ **BATCH ALL FIXES**: Collect all fixes before committing/pushing
- ✅ **SINGLE COMMIT**: All fixes committed together (not multiple commits)
- ✅ **SINGLE PUSH**: Push once after all corrections (minimal pushes)
- ✅ **CLEAN HISTORY**: Avoid multiple fix commits (batch into one)
- ✅ **BUILD TREE CLEAN**: Minimal pushes maintain clean git history

## 7.6 Early Error Detection

**Multi-Layer Validation**:
1. **Pre-commit Hooks**: Catch errors before commit (early)
2. **Post-push Agent Validation**: Comprehensive diff review (thorough)
3. **CI/CD Checks**: Automated validation on PR (continuous)

**Error Prevention**:
- ✅ Auto-fix capabilities reduce manual intervention
- ✅ Comprehensive checklists ensure nothing missed
- ✅ Multiple validation stages catch different error types
- ✅ Clear error messages guide fixes

